{
  "hero_headline": "AI产业风向突变：OpenAI延后新模型，特朗普力推行业自律 / AI Industry Shift: OpenAI Delays New Models as Trump Pushes Self-Regulation",
  "daily_overview": "科技领域，OpenAI 因安全担忧推迟新模型发布，AMD 以 82 亿美元收购 World Labs 标志着具身智能布局深化；人工智能正从单纯的「算力竞赛」向「资产效率」转型。财经层面，受美联储抗通胀政策驱动，美元走强，十年期国债收益率面临 6% 压力；与此同时，Mongolia 股市因大宗商品热潮成为全球黑马，与受 AI 波动影响的科技股形成鲜明对比。时政方面，围绕 AI 开发的全球治理博弈加剧，特朗普强调科技巨头的「自律」并排除与中国在 AI 领域开展联合研发的可能性，地缘冲突在持续拖累区域经济与工业基础。（多家报道）\n\nIn the tech sector, OpenAI has delayed new model releases due to safety concerns, while AMD’s $8.2 billion acquisition of World Labs signals a deep dive into embodied AI; the industry is shifting from a \"compute race\" to \"asset efficiency.\" On the finance front, driven by the Fed’s inflation fight, the dollar is strengthening, with 10-year Treasury yields under pressure to hit 6%. Conversely, Mongolia’s stock market is thriving on a commodity boom, contrasting with AI-linked volatility. Politically, the struggle for global AI governance is intensifying, with Trump emphasizing industry \"self-regulation\" and ruling out joint AI ventures with China, while ongoing geopolitical conflicts continue to drag on regional economies and industrial foundations.",
